{"availability":"available","full":"muhammedelsami/Toastoy","name":"Toastoy","description":"Custom Toast library","category":"Other","language":"Kotlin","stars":20,"forks":0,"created":"2023-01-13T14:50:24Z","updated":"2026-09-18T21:10:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://muhammedelsami.github.io/Toastoy/","topics":["android","android-library","kotlin","library","toast"],"demo":"https://muhammedelsami.github.io/Toastoy/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T20:16:36.070Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T20:16:36.070Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T20:16:36.070Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:36:35.049Z","stars":20,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T09:04:16.828Z","stars":20,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T00:54:55.942Z","stars":20,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T20:16:36.070Z","stars":20,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Modern, multi-line toasts for Android — one line of code, no boilerplate.","The stock Android Toast is plain, and every custom one you build yourself needs a layout, a background, an icon, and a way to survive long messages. Toastoy gives you a finished design that fits any app, and gets out of your way.","It grows to the screen width before it starts wrapping, and stays capped on tablets."],"features":["Five ready-made types — default, success, error, warning, info, each with a tinted vector icon.","Never cut off — the card hugs short messages and wraps long ones onto up to four lines.","Looks right everywhere — a dark, rounded surface that reads on both light and dark themes.","Typography you control — eight bundled variable fonts, any weight from thin to black, any size.","Multilingual — Latin, Turkish and Arabic scripts out of the box; RTL layouts supported."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/muhammedelsami/Toastoy/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f20eeb5aba5a99b648443fe5096d99d106751d7f697b9107c762d00c204c0b77","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T02:36:35.204Z"},"overviewC